From cd9c7b4873a01a28437dc812d6377939832887dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Felix=20F=C3=B6rtsch?= <mail@felixfoertsch.de>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 14:49:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ci: remove AI restrictions and set up automatic build
 pipeline

Replace upstream-only deployment tooling with validated GHCR builds for
this fork and point Compose at the fork image. Remove the inherited AI
restrictions.

Track the upstream boundary explicitly and replay the linear fork stack
on upstream develop, stopping on conflicts, empty patches, merge commits,
or upstream history rewrites. Test the replay safeguards using real local
Git repositories. Validate lint, backend tests and the frontend build
before building amd64 and arm64 candidate images.

Update the stack and upstream boundary atomically with explicit leases,
then promote the validated image to latest/develop and create a release.
Keep fork/patch-stack validation read-only until the history is activated.
Document maintenance, failure notifications and recovery in FORK.md.
---
 docker-compose.yml | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/docker-compose.yml b/docker-compose.yml
index 41c2ecd8..2b49243d 100644
--- a/docker-compose.yml
+++ b/docker-compose.yml
@@ -2,7 +2,8 @@ services:
   tubearchivist:
     container_name: tubearchivist
     restart: unless-stopped
-    image: bbilly1/tubearchivist
+    image: ghcr.io/felixfoertsch/tubearchivist:latest
+    pull_policy: always
     ports:
       - 8000:8000
     volumes:
-- 
